@page "/"

<PageTitle>Overview · TurboBoard</PageTitle>

<section class="page-heading" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
    <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
    <h1 id="overview-title">Welcome to TurboBoard</h1>
    <p>Connect trusted SQL databases, discover their structure, and build safe queries without writing SQL.</p>
</section>

<section class="card-grid" aria-label="Getting started">
    <article class="feature-card feature-card-primary">
        <span class="card-kicker">Start here</span>
        <h2>Connect your first Data Source</h2>
        <p>Data Sources keep connection details and discovered Schema metadata together in one protected workspace.</p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="data-sources">Open Data Sources</a>
    </article>

    <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Next step</span>
        <h2>Build a reusable query</h2>
        <p>Queries will turn your visual selections into validated, parameterized SQL and bounded previews.</p>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="queries">Open Queries</a>
    </article>
</section>

<section class="readiness-panel" aria-labelledby="readiness-title">
    <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Workspace readiness</span>
        <h2 id="readiness-title">A production-shaped foundation</h2>
    </div>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Server-side</strong><span>Database access remains outside the browser.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Protected state</strong><span>Local application state and encryption keys are durable.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Provider-ready</strong><span>Core query concepts stay independent of SQL Server.</span></li>
    </ul>
</section>
